From f3e690c166098697217d6c82303433d90b937bbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:39:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): command-line post mirrors a vendor .mch like the
 app

`post --machine <file>` handed the script the raw file, whose vendor
kinematics tree `script_props` cannot read, so the CLI script saw no
rotaries, spindle max, coolant codes or rates: tilted streams were
refused on tilthead.mch, and the spindle cap and coolant words were lost.
The binary now posts with `mirror(parse_mch(..))` for a vendor tree (the
app's `machine_value_for` seam); a static-grammar file posts as written,
and the raw-file inverted-axis and parse refusals run first, unchanged.

Pinned by vendor_mch_cli (tilthead tilted stream, vmc spindle cap and
mist code, both equal to the app's program).

Fixes #996

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
